542
00:37:21,440 --> 00:37:23,080
I told you to silence your phone.

543
00:37:26,560 --> 00:37:27,680
It's on me today.

544
00:37:31,920 --> 00:37:32,920
Want some popcorn?

545
00:38:35,240 --> 00:38:36,880
The male lead is hilarious.

546
00:38:48,480 --> 00:38:51,760
Those two…
are they even watching the movie?

547
00:38:54,520 --> 00:38:56,800
Hey. You can talk.

548
00:38:56,880 --> 00:38:58,360
There are barely any people here.

549
00:38:58,440 --> 00:38:59,680
No one's gonna drag you online.

550
00:39:01,200 --> 00:39:03,920
I'm not afraid of that.
I just have manners.

551
00:39:05,680 --> 00:39:06,880
Are you calling me rude?

552
00:39:14,480 --> 00:39:15,480
What are you doing?

553
00:39:16,000 --> 00:39:17,160
Taking a picture of you.

554
00:39:17,240 --> 00:39:18,320
In case people on Twitter ask

555
00:39:18,400 --> 00:39:19,840
who was being loud in the theater.

556
00:39:21,240 --> 00:39:22,240
It's X now.

557
00:39:24,680 --> 00:39:26,320
- Take it down.
- Excuse me.

558
00:39:26,400 --> 00:39:29,200
Could you keep it down?
Please be more considerate.

559
00:39:32,480 --> 00:39:33,360
This is all your fault.

560
00:39:34,800 --> 00:39:36,400
That guy's pretty handsome.

561
00:39:37,000 --> 00:39:37,920
But he's so strict.

562
00:39:38,000 --> 00:39:39,200
Because of you.

563
00:39:51,800 --> 00:39:54,480
GETTING DRAGGED

564
00:39:56,960 --> 00:39:58,480
I'm getting dragged.

565
00:40:09,160 --> 00:40:10,760
That tickles.

566
00:40:31,640 --> 00:40:34,280
Faye's here.

567
00:40:34,960 --> 00:40:36,520
How did you enjoy that movie so much?

568
00:40:38,880 --> 00:40:40,120
That was a great movie.

569
00:40:40,200 --> 00:40:41,880
Good thing we caught it
before it left cinemas.

570
00:40:41,960 --> 00:40:42,960
Yeah.

571
00:40:43,040 --> 00:40:45,440
- That was so damn good, right?
- Damn it.

572
00:40:48,160 --> 00:40:49,680
I loved it.

573
00:40:49,760 --> 00:40:52,360
If you find another movie
like this, invite me again.

574
00:40:53,320 --> 00:40:54,880
What were you two laughing about
in there anyway?

575
00:40:56,440 --> 00:40:58,480
We were talking too loudly.

576
00:40:58,560 --> 00:40:59,760
We almost got yelled at.

577
00:40:59,840 --> 00:41:02,880
Putter wrote on my hand and it tickled.

578
00:41:04,360 --> 00:41:07,320
You're crazy. You crack up so easily.

579
00:41:07,840 --> 00:41:09,920
It's not that I'm easy to amuse.

580
00:41:10,000 --> 00:41:11,520
It just really tickled.

581
00:41:11,600 --> 00:41:13,280
Faye, are you ticklish?

582
00:41:13,360 --> 00:41:14,600
- I want to write on your hand too.
- You're ticklish, aren't you?

583
00:41:16,240 --> 00:41:17,960
I'm not. Go ahead and try.

584
00:41:18,720 --> 00:41:20,280
Excuse me.

585
00:41:26,480 --> 00:41:27,880
I can't make out what you wrote.

586
00:41:28,480 --> 00:41:30,800
Well… I'm not telling.

587
00:41:37,160 --> 00:41:38,880
- Shall we get going?
- Let's go.

588
00:41:42,080 --> 00:41:43,680
Wait. "You can't read it."

589
00:41:43,760 --> 00:41:44,960
"I'm not telling."

590
00:41:45,480 --> 00:41:46,320
What's that all about?

591
00:42:02,920 --> 00:42:05,480
It's like we're playing Cupid for them.

592
00:42:05,560 --> 00:42:07,760
They're so sweet.

593
00:42:10,840 --> 00:42:12,240
Writing on hands and everything…

594
00:42:13,880 --> 00:42:14,880
What?

595
00:42:14,960 --> 00:42:16,080
Can I try again?

596
00:42:16,760 --> 00:42:18,480
- Come on.
- Want me to write on your hand again?

597
00:42:18,560 --> 00:42:19,560
No.

598
00:42:19,640 --> 00:42:20,760
I think this is easier.

599
00:42:23,520 --> 00:42:25,080
Let's write on the back.

600
00:42:25,880 --> 00:42:27,800
Na.

601
00:42:29,000 --> 00:42:30,000
Tok.

602
00:42:31,960 --> 00:42:33,120
What is it?

603
00:42:33,200 --> 00:42:34,480
No.

604
00:42:36,920 --> 00:42:38,520
Oh, "waterfall"?

605
00:42:39,960 --> 00:42:42,120
No. I wrote "You're funny."

606
00:42:43,200 --> 00:42:44,360
Now you're the one bullying me.

607
00:42:44,440 --> 00:42:45,800
You're gonna get dragged for that.

608
00:42:46,400 --> 00:42:47,920
Got any proof?

609
00:42:48,000 --> 00:42:49,400
Why wouldn't I?

610
00:42:51,840 --> 00:42:52,840
Look at this photo.

611
00:42:52,920 --> 00:42:54,320
See?

612
00:42:54,920 --> 00:42:56,760
Want to see whose internet is faster?

613
00:42:59,760 --> 00:43:02,200
That's not fair. Let's do it in our room.
We'll use the Wi-Fi.

614
00:43:03,040 --> 00:43:04,360
You're such a noob.

615
00:43:04,440 --> 00:43:07,120
That's kid stuff. Bring it on.

616
00:43:07,200 --> 00:43:08,560
Let's settle this.

617
00:43:08,640 --> 00:43:10,280
Wait for me.

618
00:43:19,600 --> 00:43:22,600
<i>I'm so happy</i>
<i>it's overflowing from my mouth.</i>

619
00:43:22,680 --> 00:43:24,560
<i>I can't even sleep on my side,</i>

620
00:43:24,640 --> 00:43:26,160
<i>or my happiness might leak out of my ears.</i>

621
00:43:27,680 --> 00:43:28,600
Hey,

622
00:43:28,680 --> 00:43:32,640
going to the movies with Faye
hit you that hard?

623
00:43:32,720 --> 00:43:34,120
Of course.

624
00:43:34,200 --> 00:43:36,560
Wow, you're literally glowing
with happiness.

625
00:43:40,960 --> 00:43:42,120
How did you guys even know?

626
00:43:42,720 --> 00:43:45,840
When the top star
and the rising star go on a date,

627
00:43:45,920 --> 00:43:47,720
of course Dispatch is all over it.

628
00:43:47,800 --> 00:43:48,720
SO INDY AND FAYE ARE TOGETHER?

629
00:43:48,800 --> 00:43:49,640
I SAW THEM AT HOUSE.

630
00:43:49,720 --> 00:43:50,680
TOP STAR AND RISING STAR ARE DATING!

631
00:43:50,760 --> 00:43:51,880
SOMEONE CAUGHT THEM PLAYING
WITH EACH OTHER'S FINGERS.

632
00:43:51,960 --> 00:43:52,800
DISPATCH, GET TO WORK!
WE NEED SOME PAPARAZZI DATING PHOTOS!

633
00:43:52,880 --> 00:43:53,840
FAYE IS USUALLY HARD TO APPROACH.
HOW DID INDY MANAGE THIS?

634
00:43:53,920 --> 00:43:54,920
AW, INDY! HE GOT TO DATE
WITH THE SCHOOL'S ANGEL.

635
00:43:55,000 --> 00:43:56,120
I'M SHIPPING THEM.
THEY REALLY SUIT EACH OTHER.

636
00:43:56,200 --> 00:43:57,400
INDY'S BEEN AFTER HER FOR A WHILE.
NEVER THOUGHT THIS SHIP WOULD SAIL.

637
00:43:58,440 --> 00:44:00,720
See? Girl power.

638
00:44:06,280 --> 00:44:07,640
Damn.

639
00:44:08,320 --> 00:44:11,440
Hey, hey. Come here.

640
00:44:11,520 --> 00:44:12,960
Did you guys hear?

641
00:44:13,040 --> 00:44:15,280
A couple is about to break up.

642
00:44:15,360 --> 00:44:16,840
What?

643
00:44:17,960 --> 00:44:19,560
Don't tell me…

644
00:44:19,640 --> 00:44:21,440
<i>This doesn't happen often.</i>

645
00:44:21,520 --> 00:44:24,080
<i>The King Class students</i>
<i>aren't studying this morning.</i>

646
00:44:24,160 --> 00:44:26,200
It's no big deal. Why make such a fuss?

647
00:44:26,280 --> 00:44:28,440
- You said, "no big deal"?
- It was only five minutes.

648
00:44:28,520 --> 00:44:29,840
Five minutes is still five minutes.

649
00:44:29,920 --> 00:44:32,120
- That was my birthday.
- The internet was down.

650
00:44:32,200 --> 00:44:34,440
Everyone else managed. Why couldn't you?

651
00:44:34,520 --> 00:44:38,480
Right now, Class 12 is on fire.

652
00:44:38,560 --> 00:44:40,200
It's more intense than Sports Day.

653
00:44:40,280 --> 00:44:41,960
They must be going at it.

654
00:44:42,920 --> 00:44:43,840
Want to go at it with me?

655
00:44:43,920 --> 00:44:44,960
Hi, babe.

656
00:44:45,040 --> 00:44:46,360
Which "babe"?

657
00:44:46,440 --> 00:44:47,680
Me or her?

658
00:44:47,760 --> 00:44:48,640
MINT: I LOVE YOU THE MOST.

659
00:44:50,160 --> 00:44:52,040
Cheating isn't funny.

660
00:44:52,120 --> 00:44:55,080
You're lowering the bar for good guys.
Right, everyone?

661
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:02,280
- Damn you, Tungtae!
- Damn you, Tungtae!

662
00:45:02,360 --> 00:45:03,680
Wait, everyone!

663
00:45:03,760 --> 00:45:05,480
Stop. Hold on.

664
00:45:07,040 --> 00:45:08,080
I'll move out of the way.

665
00:45:08,160 --> 00:45:09,920
Wait, wait, buddy.

666
00:45:10,960 --> 00:45:12,680
Why did you cheat, Tungtae?

667
00:45:12,760 --> 00:45:14,960
<i>Your friend started all this.</i>

668
00:45:22,920 --> 00:45:24,320
Damn it, Tae.

669
00:45:24,400 --> 00:45:26,080
Getting yourself blocked wasn't enough,

670
00:45:26,160 --> 00:45:28,000
now Faye blocked me too.

671
00:45:28,520 --> 00:45:30,280
I barely made it to heaven a week ago,

672
00:45:30,840 --> 00:45:31,880
and now I'm right back down at the bottom.

673
00:45:31,960 --> 00:45:33,400
It's not just you.

674
00:45:33,480 --> 00:45:34,560
We got dragged into it too.

675
00:45:34,640 --> 00:45:36,120
Both of us got lumped in with you.

676
00:45:36,200 --> 00:45:38,280
Mine's twice as bad

677
00:45:38,360 --> 00:45:40,440
because they think I'm Neo.

678
00:45:41,960 --> 00:45:43,160
What a bunch of red flags.

679
00:45:43,240 --> 00:45:44,960
Both brothers are red flags.

680
00:45:50,520 --> 00:45:51,920
What's wrong, Leo?

681
00:45:53,600 --> 00:45:55,640
What's this now?

682
00:45:56,760 --> 00:45:59,480
Now it's like
everyone is criticizing our club.

683
00:46:03,200 --> 00:46:06,760
As the club president,
I have an announcement to make.

684
00:46:06,840 --> 00:46:08,480
Go ahead, Mr. President.

685
00:46:09,000 --> 00:46:10,400
Tell us your plan.

686
00:46:10,480 --> 00:46:12,040
I don't have one yet,

687
00:46:12,840 --> 00:46:14,240
but I do have a new club rule.

688
00:46:19,240 --> 00:46:20,760
NEVER DATE ANYONE CLOSE TO YOU

689
00:46:20,840 --> 00:46:22,080
From now on,

690
00:46:22,160 --> 00:46:24,800
never date anyone close to you

691
00:46:24,880 --> 00:46:26,880
if you don't want drama in your life.

692
00:46:55,720 --> 00:46:57,760
Four pieces of chicken, no sauce, please.

693
00:46:57,840 --> 00:46:59,000
Hey,

694
00:46:59,080 --> 00:47:01,840
I think people are still
giving us weird looks.

695
00:47:05,440 --> 00:47:08,760
I think we should split up for now

696
00:47:08,840 --> 00:47:10,160
so we won't stand out.

697
00:47:11,280 --> 00:47:12,480
- Sure.
- How much is the chicken?

698
00:47:13,480 --> 00:47:14,760
- Just grab it.
- Thanks.

699
00:47:19,040 --> 00:47:20,000
Come here.

700
00:47:20,080 --> 00:47:21,200
You want Tokyo pancakes?

701
00:47:21,280 --> 00:47:22,840
- Yeah.
- Let's go.

702
00:47:22,920 --> 00:47:24,360
- Hurry up.
- Yeah, yeah.

703
00:47:24,440 --> 00:47:25,480
Let's split up.

704
00:47:27,520 --> 00:47:30,040
I'd like 30 baht
of the sweet filling, please.

705
00:47:30,120 --> 00:47:32,000
Make it extra full. Nice and sweet.

706
00:47:32,080 --> 00:47:34,840
Sure thing. I'll pack it full for you.

707
00:47:34,920 --> 00:47:35,800
Just give me a moment.

708
00:47:38,800 --> 00:47:40,440
Here you go.

709
00:47:40,520 --> 00:47:42,480
- Your order's ready.
- I'll pay by QR code.

710
00:47:42,560 --> 00:47:43,480
Sure.

711
00:47:54,960 --> 00:47:56,760
Why are you back so late, LeeIth?

712
00:47:58,720 --> 00:48:00,360
I was playing basketball with my friends.

713
00:48:01,840 --> 00:48:03,840
Until 9 p.m.?

714
00:48:03,920 --> 00:48:04,920
Isn't that a bit too late?

715
00:48:06,440 --> 00:48:08,160
I already moved out on my own.

716
00:48:08,240 --> 00:48:09,520
Are you still trying to control me?

717
00:48:11,640 --> 00:48:13,160
Just because you moved out

718
00:48:13,240 --> 00:48:14,960
doesn't mean you're all grown up.

719
00:48:16,000 --> 00:48:19,240
You still ask me for money,
and you don't even pay rent.

720
00:48:20,200 --> 00:48:22,200
So what? Did someone tell on me?

721
00:48:23,120 --> 00:48:24,560
Mom, please stop.

722
00:48:24,640 --> 00:48:25,680
See?

723
00:48:25,760 --> 00:48:27,440
Now I've argued with my mom.

724
00:48:27,960 --> 00:48:29,360
Happy now, asshole?

725
00:48:30,360 --> 00:48:31,360
LeeIth.

726
00:48:32,640 --> 00:48:33,960
Watch your mouth
when you're talking to your friend.

727
00:48:34,040 --> 00:48:36,280
Friends help each other out,
they don't act like this.

728
00:48:36,360 --> 00:48:38,720
Putter did the right thing.

729
00:48:38,800 --> 00:48:41,640
Actually, this is my room too.

730
00:48:41,720 --> 00:48:43,240
You're just staying here.

731
00:48:43,320 --> 00:48:44,960
You should listen to me too.

732
00:48:45,040 --> 00:48:45,960
LeeIth.

733
00:48:48,440 --> 00:48:49,880
Maybe I should leave

734
00:48:50,920 --> 00:48:52,480
so you two can talk.

735
00:48:53,840 --> 00:48:55,920
- Don't walk away.
- LeeIth.

736
00:48:57,880 --> 00:48:58,880
LeeIth.

737
00:49:00,480 --> 00:49:02,160
You were way out of line.

738
00:49:02,920 --> 00:49:04,960
Putter's such a nice guy.

739
00:49:05,560 --> 00:49:07,520
Friends don't rat each other out.

740
00:49:07,600 --> 00:49:10,080
And I only came home late once.

741
00:49:10,160 --> 00:49:12,520
Only once this entire month.

742
00:49:13,960 --> 00:49:15,160
I know.

743
00:49:17,000 --> 00:49:20,800
Putter already told me
you usually come back on time.

744
00:49:21,800 --> 00:49:22,960
Stop complaining.

745
00:49:24,760 --> 00:49:26,440
So why are you here today?

746
00:49:27,160 --> 00:49:29,400
I had something to do nearby,

747
00:49:29,480 --> 00:49:31,040
so I came by to see you.

748
00:49:31,120 --> 00:49:33,480
I just happened to catch you
on the day you came home late.

749
00:49:35,520 --> 00:49:36,520
So…

750
00:49:37,160 --> 00:49:38,760
Putter didn't tell you anything?

751
00:49:38,840 --> 00:49:40,360
Not a word.

752
00:49:41,120 --> 00:49:43,000
He even stood up for you,

753
00:49:43,080 --> 00:49:46,640
saying you're kind, you're a good friend,
and you're always helping people out

754
00:49:46,720 --> 00:49:49,240
with just about everything.

755
00:49:49,320 --> 00:49:50,880
He said you never go off track.

756
00:49:54,400 --> 00:49:56,120
Go bring Putter back.

757
00:50:00,320 --> 00:50:01,680
I'm going home.

758
00:50:02,320 --> 00:50:03,520
Honestly, you…

759
00:50:06,680 --> 00:50:08,320
Don't come home late again.

760
00:50:08,400 --> 00:50:10,160
- Understand?
- Yes, Mom.

761
00:50:16,360 --> 00:50:17,320
Shit.

762
00:50:48,960 --> 00:50:50,880
Please let him forgive me.

763
00:50:52,720 --> 00:50:54,280
Amen.

764
00:50:54,360 --> 00:50:56,520
Tokyo God, please grant my wish.

765
00:51:11,520 --> 00:51:13,000
Why don't you sit in the common area?

766
00:51:22,760 --> 00:51:25,000
Come on. Let's go back to our room.

767
00:51:36,280 --> 00:51:37,840
I'm sorry about earlier.

768
00:51:38,920 --> 00:51:40,200
I talked to my mom.

769
00:51:42,280 --> 00:51:43,720
You didn't tell her anything.

770
00:51:44,280 --> 00:51:45,640
You even stood up for me.

771
00:51:49,000 --> 00:51:50,160
That's right.

772
00:52:05,200 --> 00:52:07,960
Can you stop treating me like this?

773
00:52:08,760 --> 00:52:10,520
You're always smiling
around everyone else.

774
00:52:11,720 --> 00:52:13,080
Sorry.

775
00:52:13,160 --> 00:52:16,360
Sometimes I don't know
how to act around you.

776
00:52:20,800 --> 00:52:22,120
It's okay.

777
00:52:22,200 --> 00:52:24,360
I should be the one apologizing
for bothering you.

778
00:52:35,000 --> 00:52:38,480
You were just so annoying,
I wanted to mess with you.

779
00:52:39,400 --> 00:52:41,080
I never thought you were annoying.

780
00:52:42,560 --> 00:52:44,200
You just have a punchable face.

781
00:52:44,280 --> 00:52:45,360
You little…

782
00:52:56,040 --> 00:52:57,080
Let's make up.

783
00:53:00,560 --> 00:53:01,880
Please.

784
00:53:02,800 --> 00:53:04,200
Let's make up.

785
00:53:05,360 --> 00:53:06,360
Come on.

786
00:53:09,920 --> 00:53:12,200
I'm gonna fall in! I'm gonna fall in!

787
00:53:12,280 --> 00:53:13,680
What the hell are you doing?

788
00:53:16,640 --> 00:53:18,760
What was that? Look, I'm all wet.

789
00:53:20,160 --> 00:53:22,120
Yeah, that's it. Smile like that.

790
00:53:22,200 --> 00:53:24,160
Don't keep such a straight face around me.

791
00:53:24,240 --> 00:53:26,320
It's annoying. Got it?

792
00:53:27,440 --> 00:53:28,480
Thanks for telling me.

793
00:53:32,760 --> 00:53:35,600
Sometimes, I do try to adjust.

794
00:53:36,320 --> 00:53:37,960
So things won't be awkward between us.

795
00:53:38,480 --> 00:53:39,680
Okay…

796
00:53:45,440 --> 00:53:48,120
Well, I bought you something.

797
00:53:49,840 --> 00:53:51,080
It's behind you.

798
00:53:53,440 --> 00:53:54,440
Whoa.

799
00:53:55,320 --> 00:53:56,960
Sweet Tokyo pancakes.

800
00:53:59,160 --> 00:54:01,840
I love the sweet filling. Thanks.

801
00:54:03,880 --> 00:54:05,120
Eat up.

802
00:54:06,640 --> 00:54:09,600
Well, I'm heading back upstairs.

803
00:54:10,760 --> 00:54:11,840
See you in the room.

804
00:54:14,200 --> 00:54:15,080
See you.

805
00:54:36,560 --> 00:54:38,160
Why the hell is my heart racing?

806
00:54:40,360 --> 00:54:41,960
No, no, no.

807
00:54:42,040 --> 00:54:43,760
Don't fall for anyone close to you.

808
00:54:44,640 --> 00:54:45,960
LeeIth.

809
00:55:03,880 --> 00:55:05,240
CREATE - POST

810
00:55:05,320 --> 00:55:07,000
WHO CAN SEE YOUR POSTS?
CLOSE FRIENDS

811
00:55:07,080 --> 00:55:10,480
HOW DO YOU KNOW YOU'VE FALLEN FOR SOMEONE?

812
00:55:14,120 --> 00:55:15,560
<i>How?</i>

813
00:55:15,640 --> 00:55:17,240
<i>Transferring schools really got to you.</i>

814
00:55:17,320 --> 00:55:18,600
<i>What did i miss?</i>

815
00:55:21,560 --> 00:55:23,400
PUTTERRR.R
CREATE - POST

816
00:55:23,480 --> 00:55:25,520
NEXT

817
00:55:25,600 --> 00:55:28,280
WHO CAN SEE YOUR POSTS?
EVERYONE

818
00:55:28,360 --> 00:55:29,560
Sorry.

819
00:55:36,440 --> 00:55:38,040
Shit, I posted it by accident.

820
00:55:38,120 --> 00:55:39,960
Can I delete it? Is it too late?

821
00:55:42,680 --> 00:55:44,400
Shit, he already saw my story.

822
00:55:46,040 --> 00:55:47,160
Shit.

823
00:56:10,360 --> 00:56:12,960
<i>A friendly guy like Putter</i>
<i>would never like a jerk like you.</i>

824
00:56:13,040 --> 00:56:14,560
I want to know how to read someone's mind.

825
00:56:14,640 --> 00:56:16,560
Here, I got this for you.
It's your favorite.

826
00:56:16,640 --> 00:56:17,840
<i>You never act like this.</i>

827
00:56:17,920 --> 00:56:19,840
<i>We're roommates.</i>
<i>We should be close, right?</i>

828
00:56:19,920 --> 00:56:21,080
You're not very likeable.

829
00:56:22,280 --> 00:56:25,800
<i>Just imagine</i>
<i>how you'd feel if you were him.</i>

830
00:56:25,880 --> 00:56:27,760
<i>Did you cook this?</i>

831
00:56:27,840 --> 00:56:29,200
Your likability score…

832
00:56:29,280 --> 00:56:30,960
<i>I'm giving you one extra point.</i>

833
00:56:31,040 --> 00:56:34,400
Hey, have you ever had your
heart broken like Indy?

834
00:56:34,480 --> 00:56:36,640
The person I like…
